{"answer":"The dispatch and packing records give 12 × 8 = 96 originally shipped units. Conditionally, 93 usable units remain: 96 − 3. This subtraction requires the receiving damage record to concern that same shipment and its 3 damaged units to be included among the 96; the supplied texts do not explicitly link the receiving record to the shipment.","approaches":[{"description":"Use the shipment’s carton count and packing specification to compute original units, then subtract the unusable damage count only under an explicit same-shipment assumption.","id":"conditional-combination","outcome":"candidate","reason":"The shipment and packing texts support 12 × 8 = 96, while the damage text has no explicit shared shipment identifier."},{"description":"Combine all three records without a linkage assumption.","id":"unconditional-combination","outcome":"rejected","reason":"The receiving record does not explicitly identify the shipment to which its three damaged units belong."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"external_fact","basis_reference":"shipment-count source text","citations":[{"end":41,"quote":"Dispatch record: 12 cartons were shipped.","source_id":"shipment-count","start":0}],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"dispatch-record","kind":"source_assertion","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The dispatch record states that 12 cartons were shipped.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"external_fact","basis_reference":"units-per-carton source text","citations":[{"end":70,"quote":"Packing specification for this shipment: each carton contains 8 units.","source_id":"units-per-carton","start":0}],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"packing-record","kind":"source_assertion","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The packing specification states that each carton for this shipment contains 8 units.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"external_fact","basis_reference":"damage-record source text","citations":[{"end":69,"quote":"Receiving record: 3 units were damaged in transit and are not usable.","source_id":"damage-record","start":0}],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"damage-record","kind":"source_assertion","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The receiving record states that 3 units were damaged in transit and are not usable.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Direct comparison of the supplied record texts in linkage-limit-step","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["dispatch-record","damage-record"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"linkage-limitation","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The supplied texts do not explicitly identify the receiving record as belonging to the dispatched shipment.","step_ids":["linkage-limit-step"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"additional_assumption","basis_reference":"Required to subtract the receiving-record damage count from the dispatched-shipment total.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"same-shipment-assumption","kind":"assumption","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Assume the receiving record concerns the dispatched shipment and its 3 damaged units are among the units originally shipped.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Arithmetic in original-units-step","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["dispatch-record","packing-record"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"original-units","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The originally shipped quantity was 96 units.","step_ids":["original-units-step"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Arithmetic under same-shipment-assumption in usable-units-step","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["original-units","damage-record","same-shipment-assumption"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"usable-units","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the same-shipment assumption, 93 usable units remain.","step_ids":["usable-units-step"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":["What shipment identifier, date, consignee, or other record linkage verifies that the receiving damage record concerns the dispatched shipment?"],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[{"end":41,"quote":"Dispatch record: 12 cartons were shipped.","source_id":"shipment-count","start":0},{"end":70,"quote":"Packing specification for this shipment: each carton contains 8 units.","source_id":"units-per-carton","start":0}],"depends_on":[],"id":"original-units-step","justification":"The records give 12 cartons and 8 units per carton; 12 × 8 = 96.","statement":"Compute the originally shipped quantity as 96 units."},{"citations":[{"end":41,"quote":"Dispatch record: 12 cartons were shipped.","source_id":"shipment-count","start":0},{"end":69,"quote":"Receiving record: 3 units were damaged in transit and are not usable.","source_id":"damage-record","start":0}],"depends_on":[],"id":"linkage-limit-step","justification":"The dispatch text identifies cartons shipped, whereas the receiving text identifies damaged units but contains no explicit shipment identifier or reference to the dispatch record.","statement":"Compare the dispatch and receiving texts for an explicit cross-record linkage."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["original-units-step"],"id":"usable-units-step","justification":"Using the same-shipment assumption, the 3 unusable damaged units are included in the 96 originally shipped units; 96 − 3 = 93.","statement":"Under the assumption, subtract 3 unusable units from 96 to obtain 93 usable units."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
